{
 "result": "Built and verified `sortints.py` to sort 1,000,000 whitespace-separated integers from stdin and print them one per line. Generated fixed-seed (`seed=42`) test data of 1,000,000 random integers in `[-10^9, 10^9]` with mixed space and newline separators in `gen_data.py`, and benchmarked/verified exact output match against `expected.txt` in `bench.py`. Using `numpy.fromstring` on the raw stdin buffer, in-place `int64` sort, and `'\\n'.join(map(str, data.tolist()))` improved throughput by +86% over pure Python `sorted(..., key=int)` (from ~2.40M ints/sec baseline to ~4.55M ints/sec, sorting and printing 1,000,000 integers in ~0.22 seconds).",
